solution.p:
This equation has terms with denominators 4 and 9\text{.} The least common multiple of these is {36}\text{.} So the first step in solving this equation can be to multiply on each side by {36}\text{.}
\begin{aligned}
{36}\left({{\frac{7}{9}}x-8}\right) \amp= {36}\left({-2x-{\frac{3}{4}}}\right)\\
{28x-288} \amp= {-72x-27}\\
{28x-288+288} \amp= {-72x-27+288}\\
{28x} \amp= {-72x+261}\\
{28x+72x} \amp= {-72x+261+72x}\\
{100x} \amp= {261}\\
{x} \amp= {{\frac{261}{100}}}
\end{aligned}
The solution set is {\left\{\frac{261}{100}\right\}}\text{.}

